Two-GPU tensor parallelism: prior work
--------------------------------------
The tensor-parallel design in this tree descends from the following forks of
Neroued/ninfer, each licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  * Wael Mansour -- https://github.com/wamansou/ninfer-tp2-1m
    Copyright 2026 Wael Mansour. The original two-GPU tensor-parallel port:
    two-device ExecutionContext, all-reduce collectives, column- and
    row-parallel split forms of the sharded Op families, the 12/2 head-local
    attention geometry, sharded weight materialization and the two-rank
    Program wiring.

  * natpate -- https://github.com/natpate/ninfer-windows
    Native Windows build of NInfer, on which the Windows TP2 fork below builds.

  * ivanov84 -- https://github.com/ivanov84/ninfer-windows-tp2
    Native Windows TP2 and the pinned-host peer-mailbox all-reduce transport
    for GPUs without peer access.

  * parallelno -- https://github.com/parallelno/ninfer-dflash2-tp2
    DFlash2 speculative decoding at tensor-parallel width 2, per-device kernel
    attributes, mirrored rank-1 KV tables and state slots, and the per-rank
    startup memory report.

Modifications
-------------
Copyright 2026 Valerio Dolci.
Source: https://github.com/ValerioDolci/ninfer-tp2
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

This tree ports the two-GPU tensor-parallel mode onto upstream Neroued/ninfer
(commit bace20dc), largely rewritten against the upstream v3 artifact format
and execution packages. Beyond the prior work above it adds: correct
concurrent requests at tp 2 (per-lane KV binding), prefix reuse at tp 2 with
and without MTP, --spec mtp at tp 2, Vision at tp 2 (--vision-device), the
epoch-flagged PeerMailbox inside captured decode graphs, logits gathered on
rank 0, a CUDA Graph allowance sized from measurement, NVFP4 split projections
(attention and GDN input projections, row-parallel outputs) for all-NVFP4
artifacts, and the tests that qualify them. Single-GPU (--tp 1) behaviour is intended to match upstream.
The full list of changes is the git history on top of the upstream commit.

Vendored dependencies retain their own license files under third_party/.
